Z||000000||b lo 0||07-23-2000||09:27 PM||||I want to put the ZEX Automatic Nitro kit in my '85 GT... does anyone have experience with the set-up??  Also, do the V-6's have a vacuum actuated fuel pressure regulator??  And what is the TPS's output voltage?  The kit needs the vacuum thing and at least 4.2 volts on the TPS.  Thanks for any info yall can give.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>GAWD I love this car||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||07-24-2000||08:22 AM||||The ZEX kit along with the kit from Python aren't all their cracked up to be... The shop has tested them all - NOS, Nitrous Xpress, Compu Car, Nitrous Works, Python and ZEX. The best performing were the Nitrous Works Power wing kit and the NOS kit. "The engineers at ZEX and Python are trying to reinvent the wheel" according to Ed (ASE Master Tech/ ME degree from Ga. Tech, owner of the Engineered Performance) Making their shiney box regulate the input charge of nitrous to the car. where the NOS kit and The Works kit are just on and off. The best kit for a Fiero that we have seen is the Nitrous Works  part # 13093. Fuel enrichment and nitrous that is far better then the NOS kit I had. I'll get the Dyno results from the owner of the NW car and mine and post them.. we have the SAME jets .. a 40 bypass (fuel) and 42 nitrous jet. and he make a full 10hp more then me and I had an MSD box and many other mods. I'd shoot for the Nitrous Works kit.. easy to put in, from North Ga. and shiney Yellow bottle. And you can Still hook up the NOS regulator "chatter box" for a better launch.. the following is a pick of my before the NOS box and after. with nos part #05120 (.040/.042)||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||07-24-2000||08:27 AM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/progressive_1.jpg">  <P>this is with and with out the NOS progressive controller... well worth the $470! works with the NOS, Nitrous works, CompuCar and Nitrous Express kits. <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 07-24-2000).]||||reg||1
