Z||000005||HYPTNOTiSE||07-24-2000||01:22 PM||||hey 1fst2m6!  You're run with the progressive controller have you like 15 more hp? How is that possible? I'm not flaming at all, just never expected them to make a difference. Only thought it would be a good thing to elimanate tire spin and driveline wear. Can you explain, how it works and why you get more hp when using one?<P><P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
Z||000006||b lo 0||07-24-2000||01:31 PM||||1FST2M6-  I can't find a PN list on the Works site.  Which kit is that you were talking about?  I'm getting serious about this nitro thing now.<P><BR>OK, nevermind, I found it.  For GM 2.8-3.4l V6's.  One more question, how much should I plan on spending for this kit?  I don't wanna spend over $600 for a nitro kit.  Thanks again for your help guys.<BR>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>GAWD I love this car<p>[This message has been edited by b lo 0 (edited 07-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||07-24-2000||01:39 PM||||It does more than just control the  solenoids. it plugs into the computer and manipulates the fuel also.. We were all impressed with it too... I Don't know how or what it does but how it was explined in the instructions was... a delay box for the first opening (launch aid) and a milisecond(s)  adjustable chatter of the solenoids(60ft times) (yes bad for them but whatever works) in addition to lying to the computer about the impedance o the injectors forcing more fuel in to the mix.  all i did between those two runs as you can see by the time (2:38 1st run and 2:42 2nd run) between the two was flip the on/off switch and reset the cars computer. I got that part number from Nitrous Works in i think Gainsville, Ga. I've e-mailed them and thats what they told me was thier kit number. it has the special turn down for the bottle to work in the trunk of our cars and the adapter for the schrader valve/fuel pressure sensor/saftey switch. <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 07-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||07-24-2000||01:54 PM||||if and when you get a kit if you need it tuned in bring it down to the shop. We can run it in on the dyno. I'm sure they'd be happy to dialin another stop light MONSTER!   You'll love the dent you leave in the seats! <P>my kit was only a 40 hp shot but after tunig and a little messaging it was 130lbft of tq at the wheels!   HP sells cars... Torque wins races! and LOTS of them...<P>there has been a sting on Barret Parkway busting all the racing lately... not sure where its moving to yet.. working on around North Point Mall kinda in the middle of everything... Gwinnett and Cobb can all come and play...  keep me posted on the nitrous!||||reg||1
Z||000009||b lo 0||07-24-2000||02:09 PM||||Hey again.  I''ll be sure to bring it down to the shop to get it tuned.  I really need to know how much to expect to spend on this kit.  Also, I know most people use a push button, but I want to use a self-returning toggle.  This way I can get one of those spiffy red plastic safety covers so I don't go to turn on the fog lights and suddenly I'm doing 110.  Oh, also, on my way into work I got a real scare this morning.  I was going down North Druid Hills (speed limit 35) at about 55-60 mph.  This is normal for the area, but it seems today Dekalb PD was doing a little bit of a sting.  The 3 other cars I had seen pulled over should have tipped me off.  Anyways, I was in the left lane, passing a Volvo when I saw a cycle cop on the right in a side street.  Instinctively, I slammed on the brakes (gotta love 4 wheel discs).  As I passed him, he turned on his lights and pulled out.  At this point there was a big wet spot on my pants (I hate Atlanta-area traffic cops.)  I finished passing the volvo and got in front of it, hoping he would give up on me (yeah, right.)  He still had his lights on, and I thought he was gonna pass the Volvo to get to me.  Apparently he was feeling lazy (I had been doing a good 5-10 mph faster than the Volvo) because he decided to pull over the volvo.  I'm gonna drive like Grandma on the way home today!!<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>GAWD I love this car||||reg||1
