Z||000011||BBBAD GT||07-24-2000||10:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>   HP sells cars... Torque wins races! and LOTS of them...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I would say in a street race, maybe.  But at the dragstrip, HP normally can overcome gobs of torque.  <P>The best saying I've run across explaining torque/HP is <B>"Horsepower is how FAST you hit the wall, torque is how HARD"</B><BR><P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||batboy||07-24-2000||10:18 PM||||In the lower drag racing classes, torque still rules. If two equally set up cars drag raced, one with more torque and one with more horsepower, the one with more torque will have a lower ET and the one with more ponies will have a faster top speed...but the lower ET wins...simple as that. Driving on the street is a pain in the hinny if you have to do 3,000 rpm launches at every stop sign in order to keep a high hp engine with a radical cam from bogging down. Trust me on this one, I had a Chevelle SS like that once. Stop and go traffic SUCKED.||||reg||1
Z||000013||BBBAD GT||07-24-2000||10:56 PM||||I've seen way too many examples of two identical Stangs, one with around 400 rwhp and 500 rwtq (positive displacement blower), and the other being 450 rwhp and 420 rwtq (centrifugal blower), and the centrifugal one wins everytime at the strip launching with slicks.  Once past the 60' ft mark, you are basically looking at 4000+ rpms for the rest of the run.  This is where HP comes into play.   MPH is a function of HP/weight, and ET is how well you use the HP.  You can calculate HP based on your MPH/weight. There is no calculation of torque based on ET or MPH.  DOHC motors make gobs of HP, but with little torque (at least down low), but normally run better ET/MPH than a similar displacement motor of OHV or SOHC.  <P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000014||1FST2M6||07-25-2000||08:35 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I LOVE IT!  thats way better saying than mine... Stop light races is what i did more than strip runs... and the ONLY thing i lost to was a Supra turbo. but he has 600+ at the wheels.(didn't ever pick on a bike, i know i'd be toast) most the kids around here in STUPID fast moostangs cant drive unless on slicks. the tires just smoke and i'm already gone... i'm sure they're working on that now... but at the strip there are MANY faster cars.. but on the street traction plays a big role and driving ability makes a difference. on the strip... is all about both and usually who has the most wins. The weight dist. of the fiero helps you pull most cars too. I've got a Procharger still in a box if anyones looking for one.. Had it for a while and i'ts never been spun. will fit where the a/c was you'd have to figure out the rest of the bracketry and piping... Tried to return it to the original retailer but since its a special order part i'm stuck with it...  ||||reg||1
